From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Circuit-Sword Batocera port <local@circuit-sword>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linux-user: fix redefinition of struct sched_attr

QEMU's linux-user/syscall.c unconditionally defines its own
struct sched_attr, with the comment "sched_attr is not defined in
glibc". On newer host toolchains (as used by the Buildroot Docker
build container), linux/sched/types.h now provides this struct
itself, causing a hard redefinition error:

  linux-user/syscall.c:363:8: error: redefinition of 'struct sched_attr'
  ...
  /usr/include/linux/sched/types.h:98:8: note: originally defined here

Guard QEMU's own definition behind SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER0, the size
macro the kernel UAPI header defines alongside struct sched_attr,
so QEMU only provides its own copy when the system headers don't
already have one.

Not yet submitted upstream — local fix for this build.

Signed-off-by: Circuit-Sword Batocera port <local@circuit-sword>
---
 linux-user/syscall.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/linux-user/syscall.c
+++ b/linux-user/syscall.c
@@ -360,6 +360,7 @@
 _syscall3(int, sys_sched_setaffinity, pid_t, pid, unsigned int, len,
           unsigned long *, user_mask_ptr);
 /* sched_attr is not defined in glibc */
+#ifndef SCHED_ATTR_SIZE_VER0
 struct sched_attr {
     uint32_t size;
     uint32_t sched_policy;
@@ -372,6 +373,7 @@
     uint32_t sched_util_min;
     uint32_t sched_util_max;
 };
+#endif
 #define __NR_sys_sched_getattr __NR_sched_getattr
 _syscall4(int, sys_sched_getattr, pid_t, pid, struct sched_attr *, attr,
           unsigned int, size, unsigned int, flags);
